%S A399502 0,1,1,3,4,4,3,4,4,6,7,7,9,10,10,9,10,10,15,16,16,18,19,19,18,19,19,
%T A399502 21,22,22,24,25,25,24,25,25,27,28,28,30,31,31,30,31,31,33,34,34,36,37,
%U A399502 37,36,37,37,36,37,37,39,40,40,39,40,40,42,43,43,45,46,46
%N A399502 Consider a 3D sandpile model where each site with 3 or more grains, say at location (x, y, z), topples and transfers one grain of sand to the sites at locations (x+1, y, z), (x, y+1, z) and (x, y, z+1); a(n) gives the number of nonempty sites after stabilization of a configuration starting with n grains at the origin.
%C A399502 Sites containing 0, 1 or 2 grains are stable.
%C A399502 After stabilization, there are:
%C A399502 - 2*a(n) - n sites with one grain,
%C A399502 - n - a(n) sites with two grains.
%H A399502 Rémy Sigrist, <a href="/A399502/b399502.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%H A399502 Rémy Sigrist, <a href="https://practical-ardinghelli-959d8f.netlify.app/a399502">Interactive representation of the envelope of the stabilized configuration for n = 2^20</a> [provided your web browser supports the Plotly library, you should see icons on the top right corner of the page: if you choose "Orbital rotation", then you will be able to rotate the plot alongside three axes]
%H A399502 Rémy Sigrist, <a href="/A399502/a399502.png">Top view of the stabilized configuration for n = 2^20</a> (blue and red pixels correspond to sites with 1 and 2 grains, respectively)
%H A399502 Rémy Sigrist, <a href="/A399502/a399502.gp.txt">PARI program</a>
%H A399502 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abelian_sandpile_model#Sandpile_models_on_directed_graphs">Sandpile models on directed graphs</a>
%F A399502 a(3*n) + 1 = a(3*n + 1) = a(3*n + 2).
%e A399502 For n = 42: the sites, before and after toppling, are, layer by layer:
%e A399502    x+y+z  before toppling  after toppling  nonempty
%e A399502    -----  ---------------  --------------  --------
%e A399502      0          42               .                0
%e A399502 .
%e A399502      1        14  14            2 2               3
%e A399502                 14               2
%e A399502 .
%e A399502      2         4 8 4           1 2 1              6
%e A399502                 8 8             2 2
%e A399502                  4               1
%e A399502 .
%e A399502      3        1 3 3 1         1 . . 1             3
%e A399502                3 6 3           . . .
%e A399502                 3 3             . .
%e A399502                  1               1
%e A399502 .
%e A399502      4       . 1 2 1 .       . 1 2 1 .           12
%e A399502               1 4 4 1         1 1 1 1
%e A399502                2 4 2           2 1 2
%e A399502                 1 1             1 1
%e A399502                  .               .
%e A399502 .
%e A399502      5      . . . . . .     . . . . . .           6
%e A399502              . 1 2 1 .       . 1 2 1 .
%e A399502               . 2 2 .         . 2 2 .
%e A399502                . 1 .           . 1 .
%e A399502                 . .             . .
%e A399502                  .               .
%e A399502 .
%e A399502 So a(42) = 0 + 3 + 6 + 3 + 12 + 6 = 30.
